        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2^{-2}=\\dfrac14$; $-2^2=-4$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2^{-2}&=\\frac{1}{2^2}\\\\&=\\frac14\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}-2^2&=-(2^2)\\\\&=-4\\end{align*}$$\nA negative exponent gives a reciprocal. In $-2^2$, the power is evaluated before the negative sign.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
